1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,837
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor… ♪

2
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:06,172
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

3
00:00:09,342 --> 00:00:10,468
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor… ♪

4
00:00:10,552 --> 00:00:12,846
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

5
00:00:12,929 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ One cut and it's over ♪

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:20,228
SAMIR: Tell me who was hired
to rescue the Belladonna.

7
00:00:20,311 --> 00:00:21,604
The Firefighter.

8
00:00:21,688 --> 00:00:23,565
ARTEM: That's Uno Alcaraz.

9
00:00:23,648 --> 00:00:25,817
Then we must go right now
and get him.

10
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:27,193
I need to talk to Uno.

11
00:00:27,277 --> 00:00:29,821
NURSE: Someone is shooting
in patient Alcaraz’s room!

12
00:00:29,904 --> 00:00:31,364
The cop who was guarding him
is already dead.

13
00:00:31,448 --> 00:00:33,241
[gunshots]

14
00:00:33,324 --> 00:00:34,743
[bullets whizzing]

15
00:00:34,826 --> 00:00:36,786
[music continues]

16
00:00:36,870 --> 00:00:38,496
SAMIR: Artem, take the fire exit.

17
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:39,914
We need Uno Alacaraz.

18
00:00:39,998 --> 00:00:41,916
I'll stay here and handle these two. Go!

19
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,460
[grunting & groaning]

20
00:00:43,835 --> 00:00:45,628
[thumping & thudding]

21
00:00:45,712 --> 00:00:46,880
[bullets whizzes]

22
00:00:46,963 --> 00:00:47,922
[gunshots]

23
00:00:48,006 --> 00:00:49,507
ELIAS: Oop! Stop!

24
00:00:49,591 --> 00:00:50,258
Who are you?

25
00:00:50,341 --> 00:00:51,342
Face this way,

26
00:00:51,426 --> 00:00:52,761
remove your mask!

27
00:00:52,844 --> 00:00:54,054
[clinks]

28
00:00:54,137 --> 00:00:55,013
[swooshes, clangs, then hisses]

29
00:00:55,096 --> 00:00:56,347
JANINE: Let’s join the dance club!

30
00:00:56,431 --> 00:00:57,015
Are you joining?

31
00:00:57,098 --> 00:00:58,892
You need to audition as a trio.

32
00:00:58,975 --> 00:01:00,602
What dance po?

33
00:01:00,685 --> 00:01:01,728
Anything.

34
00:01:01,811 --> 00:01:02,604
Where’s Uno?

35
00:01:02,687 --> 00:01:04,064
I didn't see him.

36
00:01:04,147 --> 00:01:05,648
I really hope he managed to escape.

37
00:01:05,732 --> 00:01:07,650
Don't tell Audrey what happened.

38
00:01:07,734 --> 00:01:09,611
I'm with Oscar at the hospital now.

39
00:01:09,694 --> 00:01:10,653
[weapon swishes]

40
00:01:10,737 --> 00:01:13,239
Audrey: He was stabbed while saving me.

41
00:01:13,323 --> 00:01:14,199
Oscar: Sorry, to you,

42
00:01:14,282 --> 00:01:16,409
to all of you who were there.
It's so embarrassing, really.

43
00:01:16,493 --> 00:01:17,619
Don't worry about that,

44
00:01:17,702 --> 00:01:18,912
I'll take care of them.

45
00:01:18,995 --> 00:01:20,538
Atoy again and again?

46
00:01:20,622 --> 00:01:22,832
Artem: We must kill that guy.

47
00:01:22,916 --> 00:01:23,625
He's a pest.

48
00:01:23,708 --> 00:01:24,959
He will have his day.

49
00:01:25,043 --> 00:01:26,252
Audrey: Maybe you'd like…

50
00:01:26,336 --> 00:01:27,587
to stay with us for now?

51
00:01:27,670 --> 00:01:29,756
I thought I wasn't welcome there? Right?

52
00:01:29,839 --> 00:01:30,882
I thought you didn't like me?

53
00:01:30,965 --> 00:01:32,801
To make it up to you.

54
00:01:32,884 --> 00:01:34,010
Janine: What happened, Ibyang?

55
00:01:34,093 --> 00:01:35,929
Why are your steps wrong again?

56
00:01:36,012 --> 00:01:37,972
Because it's really hard.

57
00:01:38,056 --> 00:01:40,058
Audrey: Uhm, did you leave behind

58
00:01:40,141 --> 00:01:42,060
a girlfriend or wife?

59
00:01:42,143 --> 00:01:43,686
My type is different now too, you know.

60
00:01:43,770 --> 00:01:45,021
[music continues]

61
00:01:45,104 --> 00:01:46,898
You, maybe you have a sister, Audrey.

62
00:01:46,981 --> 00:01:47,857
Ah, no.

63
00:01:47,941 --> 00:01:50,026
Audrey has no sister.

64
00:01:50,693 --> 00:01:51,820
Too bad.

65
00:01:54,322 --> 00:01:55,615
[music fades]

66
00:01:56,116 --> 00:01:58,785
Lord, thank you so much

67
00:01:58,868 --> 00:01:59,619
for our food,

68
00:01:59,702 --> 00:02:02,288
and for all your blessings
You have given us, Lord.

69
00:02:03,123 --> 00:02:05,208
Oscar: I also want to give thanks

70
00:02:05,291 --> 00:02:07,210
to Atoy, to Audrey,

71
00:02:08,294 --> 00:02:09,212
because of them I found…

72
00:02:09,295 --> 00:02:12,924
my new family, Lord, thank you.

73
00:02:13,383 --> 00:02:14,384
All: Amen.

74
00:02:14,467 --> 00:02:15,593
Amen, amen!

75
00:02:15,677 --> 00:02:17,220
Okay, all right.

76
00:02:17,303 --> 00:02:18,847
Others: Eat! Let's eat!
Let's eat, let's eat.

77
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:20,140
Child, do you want…

78
00:02:20,223 --> 00:02:22,475
Ah, Oscar, what are you planning to do

79
00:02:22,559 --> 00:02:24,435
while you're staying here?

80
00:02:24,519 --> 00:02:26,980
Do you already have a job in mind?

81
00:02:27,063 --> 00:02:30,316
Yes, uhm, Miss Cita, I'll apply.

82
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:31,025
There are so many,

83
00:02:31,109 --> 00:02:32,527
so many jobs that Oka could take.

84
00:02:32,610 --> 00:02:33,903
[utensils clatter]

85
00:02:33,987 --> 00:02:35,738
There, look! A food trip place!

86
00:02:35,822 --> 00:02:37,115
- Oh, 'Son!
- Wow! Idol!

87
00:02:37,198 --> 00:02:38,116
Let's eat, let's eat. Come.
Let's eat!

88
00:02:38,199 --> 00:02:39,450
- Perfect timing. I'll join you.
- Come on, okay.

89
00:02:39,534 --> 00:02:40,160
Miss Cita, please stand up first.

90
00:02:40,243 --> 00:02:42,996
There.
[lively chatter & laughing]

91
00:02:43,079 --> 00:02:44,706
Perfect. There!

92
00:02:44,789 --> 00:02:46,875
[lively chatter]

93
00:02:46,958 --> 00:02:48,209
[music continues]

94
00:02:48,293 --> 00:02:50,086
Just get it from there.
You know where it is.

95
00:02:50,169 --> 00:02:51,045
Emerson: Okay.

96
00:02:51,129 --> 00:02:52,547
[utensils clatter]

97
00:02:52,630 --> 00:02:54,340
- Oka.
- Emerson.

98
00:02:54,424 --> 00:02:55,425
Please pass me some rice.

99
00:02:55,508 --> 00:02:57,176
What happened to your… shoulder?

100
00:02:57,260 --> 00:02:58,344
Emerson: You're injured.

101
00:02:58,428 --> 00:02:59,429
Did you get in trouble again?

102
00:02:59,512 --> 00:03:00,388
Ame: Hey, Emerson!

103
00:03:00,471 --> 00:03:02,932
What are you here for?
To eat or to gossip?

104
00:03:03,016 --> 00:03:03,892
I'm just asking.

105
00:03:04,392 --> 00:03:09,022
Oka, Emerson has set up a new business.
Oka: Mmm?

106
00:03:09,105 --> 00:03:10,773
His investigation agency.

107
00:03:10,857 --> 00:03:11,774
The Children of the Thread.

108
00:03:11,858 --> 00:03:14,235
Oh, Emerson, maybe there's
an opening in your agency,

109
00:03:14,319 --> 00:03:15,737
maybe Oka can apply.

110
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:16,821
Right?

111
00:03:16,905 --> 00:03:17,947
Oh, he’s very good.

112
00:03:18,031 --> 00:03:21,784
Ahh. Yes-- ah, yes, okay--
Yes, he can.

113
00:03:21,868 --> 00:03:24,829
At the-- the office. Ah, okay.
Go to the office, apply at the office.

114
00:03:25,538 --> 00:03:26,706
[music continues]

115
00:03:26,789 --> 00:03:29,000
Sorry, Emerson, maybe
I’ll apply somewhere else instead.

116
00:03:29,083 --> 00:03:30,293
No offense, no offense, but--

117
00:03:31,127 --> 00:03:32,754
Audrey, maybe at your, at…

118
00:03:33,504 --> 00:03:34,756
at your company, maybe there's an opening?

119
00:03:34,839 --> 00:03:37,842
Actually, Harvest Aid is hiring now.

120
00:03:37,926 --> 00:03:39,719
They're looking for a driver.

121
00:03:40,261 --> 00:03:42,222
But you probably don’t want
that kind of job.

122
00:03:42,305 --> 00:03:43,806
No-- geez. That's fine!

123
00:03:43,890 --> 00:03:44,641
Perfectly fine!

124
00:03:44,724 --> 00:03:45,850
And any…

125
00:03:45,934 --> 00:03:47,685
kind of vehicle I can drive.

126
00:03:47,769 --> 00:03:48,853
Are you sure?

127
00:03:48,937 --> 00:03:50,230
Pshh.

128
00:03:50,313 --> 00:03:50,855
Audrey: All right.

129
00:03:50,939 --> 00:03:52,899
[utensils clattering]

130
00:03:52,982 --> 00:03:54,609
Where's the ketchup?

131
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:56,194
Yes?

132
00:03:57,070 --> 00:03:57,904
The ketchup? Here.

133
00:03:57,987 --> 00:03:58,488
Here.

134
00:03:58,571 --> 00:03:59,489
- I'll-- I'll get it.
- No, I'll get it.

135
00:03:59,572 --> 00:04:02,867
- No, I'll get it. No, I'll get it.
- I'm closer, you know.

136
00:04:02,951 --> 00:04:04,827
[clamoring]
Audrey: Oh, oh-- ah-- oh!

137
00:04:04,911 --> 00:04:05,453
[gasps]

138
00:04:05,536 --> 00:04:06,788
What a waste of ketchup, look.

139
00:04:06,871 --> 00:04:09,123
What’s wrong with you?
You two are so clumsy!

140
00:04:09,207 --> 00:04:10,625
So-- sorry.
[coughs]

141
00:04:10,708 --> 00:04:11,459
Here it is, look.

142
00:04:11,542 --> 00:04:13,378
- Oh-- no, I-- I'll get it.
- Here, here, here, here.

143
00:04:13,461 --> 00:04:14,837
[panicking]
Oop, oop, oop, oop, oop!

144
00:04:14,921 --> 00:04:17,590
I'll get it, I'll get it. I'll get it.

145
00:04:17,674 --> 00:04:18,174
[pensive music playing]

146
00:04:18,258 --> 00:04:20,677
What happened, huh? Let's change.
Come, let's change clothes.

147
00:04:20,760 --> 00:04:21,386
Come on.

148
00:04:21,469 --> 00:04:22,095
I'll be back, child, okay.

149
00:04:22,178 --> 00:04:23,346
Come.

150
00:04:25,390 --> 00:04:26,849
[music fades]

151
00:04:26,933 --> 00:04:28,935
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

152
00:04:29,936 --> 00:04:32,272
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor… ♪

153
00:04:32,355 --> 00:04:34,315
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

154
00:04:38,278 --> 00:04:39,737
♪ Wait a moment, Mr. Tailor ♪

155
00:04:39,821 --> 00:04:41,823
♪ Can you be the one to stitch up ♪

156
00:04:41,906 --> 00:04:45,201
♪ The hole in my polo that's right
under the armpit ♪

157
00:04:45,285 --> 00:04:47,453
♪ In every cut of cloth ♪

158
00:04:47,537 --> 00:04:49,205
♪ There’s a secret behind it ♪

159
00:04:49,289 --> 00:04:51,207
♪ If your measurements are wrong,

160
00:04:51,291 --> 00:04:56,254
the whole fit turns crooked… ♪

161
00:04:56,337 --> 00:04:56,963
[gunshots]

162
00:04:57,046 --> 00:04:58,715
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor ♪

163
00:04:58,798 --> 00:05:00,883
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

164
00:05:00,967 --> 00:05:02,176
[music swells]

165
00:05:05,388 --> 00:05:06,306
[music fades]

166
00:05:07,098 --> 00:05:10,351
[hip-hop upbeat music playing]

167
00:05:10,435 --> 00:05:11,227
[whoops]

168
00:05:11,311 --> 00:05:12,895
[music continues]

169
00:05:18,901 --> 00:05:21,154
Audrey: That's awesome!

170
00:05:21,237 --> 00:05:22,947
All together!

171
00:05:23,031 --> 00:05:25,700
[lively chatter]

172
00:05:25,783 --> 00:05:26,617
[music continues]

173
00:05:27,660 --> 00:05:28,328
Okay.

174
00:05:28,411 --> 00:05:28,953
How? How? How?

175
00:05:29,037 --> 00:05:30,371
Miss, join us.

176
00:05:30,455 --> 00:05:31,956
Miss Cita!

177
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:33,708
Miss Cita, come!

178
00:05:33,791 --> 00:05:34,334
Yiee!

179
00:05:34,417 --> 00:05:36,044
- Audrey: Oh, how's that?
- How's the step, child?

180
00:05:36,127 --> 00:05:36,627
What do we do?

181
00:05:36,711 --> 00:05:38,588
[lively chatter]

182
00:05:38,671 --> 00:05:40,631
[suspicious music playing]

183
00:05:41,132 --> 00:05:41,966
Wow!

184
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:42,884
Oh, you next!

185
00:05:42,967 --> 00:05:43,760
You next!

186
00:05:43,843 --> 00:05:44,969
Next step you, next--

187
00:05:45,803 --> 00:05:52,727
[lively chatter]

188
00:05:56,981 --> 00:05:58,232
Audrey: Miss Cita, Miss Cita!

189
00:05:58,316 --> 00:06:00,943
Show us your moves. Show us.
[Audrey chuckles]

190
00:06:01,027 --> 00:06:04,322
'Toy, can I talk to you for a moment?

191
00:06:04,906 --> 00:06:05,823
Okay.

192
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:09,911
[lively chatter]

193
00:06:09,994 --> 00:06:12,038
[tense music playing]

194
00:06:13,623 --> 00:06:14,999
'Son, what’s up?

195
00:06:15,666 --> 00:06:16,959
No, it's, ah--

196
00:06:17,043 --> 00:06:20,755
Karla already told me about Uno.

197
00:06:20,838 --> 00:06:22,423
She said he's missing.

198
00:06:22,507 --> 00:06:23,674
Did he escape?

199
00:06:24,967 --> 00:06:28,304
Yes. I need to find Uno,
before Samir finds him.

200
00:06:28,971 --> 00:06:31,682
I have a feeling he knows
more about the Belladonna.

201
00:06:31,766 --> 00:06:33,017
You know, 'Toy…

202
00:06:34,102 --> 00:06:35,478
I'll take charge of finding Uno.

203
00:06:35,561 --> 00:06:36,521
Entrust him to me,

204
00:06:36,604 --> 00:06:38,022
I'll bring him to you.

205
00:06:38,106 --> 00:06:40,691
Because anyway, I know you're retired
from being a tracker and all that.

206
00:06:40,775 --> 00:06:43,152
I'll take care of that, yes.

207
00:06:43,236 --> 00:06:44,737
Just tell me.

208
00:06:45,279 --> 00:06:46,364
Ah, but,

209
00:06:47,115 --> 00:06:48,699
in order for me to do that…

210
00:06:50,618 --> 00:06:51,911
where does he live?

211
00:06:51,994 --> 00:06:53,371
Ah, does he have social media?

212
00:06:53,454 --> 00:06:55,039
Does he have a family?

213
00:06:55,123 --> 00:06:56,707
Ah, does he have a favorite quote,

214
00:06:56,791 --> 00:06:57,416
favorite color.

215
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:58,793
I need those details, you see, eh--

216
00:06:58,876 --> 00:07:00,628
- Maybe you have some leads.
- Atoy: 'Son…

217
00:07:00,711 --> 00:07:01,879
But I'll handle it.

218
00:07:01,963 --> 00:07:03,131
I appreciate that.

219
00:07:03,214 --> 00:07:03,714
Emerson: Okay.

220
00:07:03,798 --> 00:07:05,174
But leave him be,

221
00:07:05,258 --> 00:07:06,134
he's just cooling off.

222
00:07:06,968 --> 00:07:09,178
Okay? Don't-- don't--
Let's not disturb him.

223
00:07:09,929 --> 00:07:11,806
Eh… But why?

224
00:07:11,889 --> 00:07:13,266
Will he come here? What do you think?

225
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:17,770
Uno is smart, he won't come here.

226
00:07:18,438 --> 00:07:19,564
Because he knows…

227
00:07:20,064 --> 00:07:22,400
if he comes, wherever he goes,

228
00:07:22,483 --> 00:07:24,026
Samir will follow him.

229
00:07:24,110 --> 00:07:25,111
He won't do that.

230
00:07:26,821 --> 00:07:28,197
He won't put me in danger.

231
00:07:29,365 --> 00:07:30,575
Okay.

232
00:07:30,658 --> 00:07:31,492
[clicks tongue]

233
00:07:31,993 --> 00:07:34,078
You know, since you mentioned that.

234
00:07:34,162 --> 00:07:36,831
Speaking of, ah, danger.

235
00:07:36,914 --> 00:07:38,124
[suspicious music playing]

236
00:07:39,584 --> 00:07:41,127
Why did you let Oscar come back?

237
00:07:42,295 --> 00:07:44,422
[music continues]

238
00:07:45,715 --> 00:07:46,632
Oh?

239
00:07:47,216 --> 00:07:48,342
Bro, ah. Just this, ah…

240
00:07:48,426 --> 00:07:49,635
- This is just my opinion.
- Oh, what is it?

241
00:07:49,719 --> 00:07:53,139
I get a different vibe from him.
I have a different feeling, bro.

242
00:07:53,222 --> 00:07:54,307
There's something I don't…

243
00:07:54,390 --> 00:07:55,766
[clicks tongue]
You know?

244
00:07:56,350 --> 00:07:58,769
I just couldn't tell you before but…

245
00:07:59,687 --> 00:08:02,064
I think he's kind of not good, you know.

246
00:08:02,899 --> 00:08:04,692
Yeah. And also, ah, when--

247
00:08:04,775 --> 00:08:08,237
I noticed he looks at all of you.

248
00:08:08,321 --> 00:08:10,656
Like, bro, it's like there is
a hint of… envy.

249
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:11,824
Atoy: Bro, bro…

250
00:08:13,326 --> 00:08:15,286
you just resent him

251
00:08:15,369 --> 00:08:18,956
because he didn't join your group,
Children of the Thread!

252
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:20,124
Well, he's not qualified either.

253
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,502
Why, though?
[clicks tongue]

254
00:08:22,585 --> 00:08:27,173
Emerson, if you just get to know Oscar,

255
00:08:27,715 --> 00:08:29,342
you'd get along with him.

256
00:08:29,425 --> 00:08:31,177
He's kind!

257
00:08:31,260 --> 00:08:34,680
I don't want him to feel like
he's unwelcome here in Tabang Lupa.

258
00:08:34,764 --> 00:08:36,390
Atoy: Because of course he's my friend,

259
00:08:36,474 --> 00:08:38,559
and my family too now.

260
00:08:40,061 --> 00:08:42,939
[anxious music playing]

261
00:08:48,319 --> 00:08:51,948
[music continues]

262
00:09:16,806 --> 00:09:19,308
Kiss me, My Love.

263
00:09:21,894 --> 00:09:24,063
[music continues]

264
00:09:26,107 --> 00:09:29,318
[applauds]

265
00:09:29,402 --> 00:09:30,945
Oka!

266
00:09:31,028 --> 00:09:32,154
- Hey!
- Oh?

267
00:09:32,238 --> 00:09:33,614
Looks like you zoned out there.

268
00:09:33,698 --> 00:09:34,365
Are you okay?

269
00:09:34,448 --> 00:09:36,617
- Come, join us.
- It's okay, I'm okay.

270
00:09:37,368 --> 00:09:39,787
Well, uhm, actually…

271
00:09:39,870 --> 00:09:41,205
everything is clear to me now.

272
00:09:42,331 --> 00:09:43,332
There are…

273
00:09:44,667 --> 00:09:48,546
good things I just realized that
I want to happen in my life.

274
00:09:48,629 --> 00:09:50,506
[lively chatter]

275
00:09:51,132 --> 00:09:52,300
I hope…

276
00:09:53,217 --> 00:09:54,635
that comes true for you.

277
00:09:54,719 --> 00:09:55,678
Oscar: Mmm-hmm.

278
00:09:55,761 --> 00:09:57,346
[lively chatter]

279
00:09:57,430 --> 00:09:58,222
Audrey: You know what?

280
00:09:59,348 --> 00:10:01,350
You deserve a new and better life.

281
00:10:01,434 --> 00:10:04,145
[music continues]

282
00:10:04,228 --> 00:10:04,937
Join us.

283
00:10:05,479 --> 00:10:06,105
Oscar: It's okay.

284
00:10:06,856 --> 00:10:07,898
Ah, I'll just watch.

285
00:10:08,941 --> 00:10:09,775
Audrey: Sure?

286
00:10:09,859 --> 00:10:10,484
Yeah.

287
00:10:10,568 --> 00:10:11,611
[lively chatter]

288
00:10:11,694 --> 00:10:14,488
Are you okay with coffee?
Do you need anything else?

289
00:10:14,572 --> 00:10:15,698
- Come on, Mama.
- Okay, okay.

290
00:10:15,781 --> 00:10:16,949
[music continues]

291
00:10:17,033 --> 00:10:17,950
[lively chatter]
Audrey: Okay.

292
00:10:18,034 --> 00:10:22,622
What's the second step besides mmm-hmm.

293
00:10:22,705 --> 00:10:25,124
[lively chatter]

294
00:10:25,207 --> 00:10:27,793
I'll make sure
all of that happens, Audrey,

295
00:10:28,794 --> 00:10:31,505
and Atoy won't be able to do anything.

296
00:10:31,589 --> 00:10:33,549
[tense music playing]

297
00:10:33,633 --> 00:10:35,926
Hey, hey, hey.

298
00:10:36,010 --> 00:10:40,389
[gasps]
[lively chatter]

299
00:10:40,473 --> 00:10:41,849
Others: Hey!

300
00:10:41,932 --> 00:10:44,101
[chuckles]
[lively chatter]

301
00:10:48,648 --> 00:10:52,818
[sneaky music playing]

302
00:10:54,779 --> 00:10:58,407
[music continues]

303
00:11:15,299 --> 00:11:16,759
[knocks]

304
00:11:17,718 --> 00:11:18,594
Knock, knock!

305
00:11:18,677 --> 00:11:20,221
Hey. What are you doing here?

306
00:11:20,304 --> 00:11:21,263
You're not allowed here.

307
00:11:21,347 --> 00:11:22,932
Sir, ah, it's Emerson, by the way.

308
00:11:23,015 --> 00:11:24,683
Sorry to disturb you.

309
00:11:24,767 --> 00:11:28,938
I just want to ask a favor
because my nephew is, ah, uhm…

310
00:11:29,021 --> 00:11:31,690
Uno Alcaraz, the one who
was ambushed the other day.

311
00:11:31,774 --> 00:11:33,734
Yes, the one in 415.

312
00:11:33,818 --> 00:11:34,485
So…

313
00:11:34,568 --> 00:11:37,154
Sorry, we still haven't found him
until now.

314
00:11:37,238 --> 00:11:39,031
Our family is already worried.

315
00:11:39,115 --> 00:11:40,074
I'm here to ask if maybe…

316
00:11:40,157 --> 00:11:43,577
maybe I could take a look at…

317
00:11:43,661 --> 00:11:44,870
your security footage,

318
00:11:44,954 --> 00:11:47,248
just to see where he ran.

319
00:11:47,331 --> 00:11:50,668
Oh, we don't show our
security footage to just anyone.

320
00:11:51,669 --> 00:11:54,004
Even the police need an official request.

321
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:56,632
Ahh. Is that so?

322
00:11:56,715 --> 00:11:57,633
Oh, okay, sir.

323
00:11:57,716 --> 00:11:59,427
- You're not allowed here.
- Too bad.

324
00:11:59,510 --> 00:12:00,886
Yes.

325
00:12:00,970 --> 00:12:02,388
[sneaky music playing]

326
00:12:02,471 --> 00:12:04,014
Okay, yes.

327
00:12:04,098 --> 00:12:05,891
[music continues]

328
00:12:05,975 --> 00:12:06,809
Uhm…

329
00:12:06,892 --> 00:12:08,352
Okay, sir, ah, I'll go ahead.

330
00:12:08,436 --> 00:12:09,186
- Sorry for the--
- Oh!

331
00:12:09,270 --> 00:12:10,020
- Oh, so-- so-- so--
- It's hot!

332
00:12:10,104 --> 00:12:11,814
- Sorry. Oh, sorry.
- Aargh!

333
00:12:11,897 --> 00:12:13,566
- Sorry, sorry, sorry, sorry.
- It's hot!

334
00:12:13,649 --> 00:12:14,775
Sorry, huh.

335
00:12:14,859 --> 00:12:16,235
Ah, I'll go ahead. Sorry.

336
00:12:16,318 --> 00:12:17,862
I’m really sorry, really sorry.

337
00:12:17,945 --> 00:12:19,029
[playful music playing]

338
00:12:24,743 --> 00:12:26,328
I got burned too.

339
00:12:26,412 --> 00:12:27,079
[scoffs]

340
00:12:27,163 --> 00:12:28,706
It's so sticky.

341
00:12:28,789 --> 00:12:29,665
Annoying.

342
00:12:29,748 --> 00:12:32,209
[sneaky music playing]

343
00:12:44,054 --> 00:12:46,974
You thought you could hide something
from the Children of the Thread, huh.

344
00:12:47,057 --> 00:12:49,226
[music continues]

345
00:13:01,989 --> 00:13:04,867
[keyboard clacking]

346
00:13:04,950 --> 00:13:07,953
[music continues]

347
00:13:08,537 --> 00:13:09,997
Gotcha.

348
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:11,916
[music continues]

349
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:16,545
Oh? Have you seen the footage
that I asked from you?

350
00:13:16,629 --> 00:13:17,421
[music fades]

351
00:13:18,255 --> 00:13:19,590
[clears throat]

352
00:13:20,216 --> 00:13:21,425
Ah, what was that again…

353
00:13:21,509 --> 00:13:23,093
what footage, Sir?

354
00:13:23,761 --> 00:13:24,762
Elias: That…

355
00:13:24,845 --> 00:13:26,639
There, that! That exact one!

356
00:13:26,722 --> 00:13:28,307
What you're looking at now.

357
00:13:28,390 --> 00:13:30,059
[sneaky music playing]

358
00:13:30,142 --> 00:13:31,435
Ah, oh-- oh, okay po, okay.

359
00:13:31,519 --> 00:13:34,605
Ah, wait a moment, I'll just get…

360
00:13:34,688 --> 00:13:36,565
a diskette from…

361
00:13:36,649 --> 00:13:37,483
the stock room.

362
00:13:37,566 --> 00:13:39,652
Ha, so I can save it there.
Wait a minute.

363
00:13:39,735 --> 00:13:40,736
Just a moment.

364
00:13:40,819 --> 00:13:42,821
[music continues]

365
00:13:44,406 --> 00:13:46,951
Sir, what's a diskette?

366
00:13:47,034 --> 00:13:48,035
[music fades]

367
00:13:48,118 --> 00:13:49,119
Diskette.

368
00:13:50,162 --> 00:13:52,122
[pleasant music playing]

369
00:13:52,206 --> 00:13:53,290
Wait, wait.

370
00:13:53,374 --> 00:13:54,583
Go after him, chase him!

371
00:13:54,667 --> 00:13:55,417
The diskette?

372
00:13:55,501 --> 00:13:57,253
No! The guy-- let’s just go!

373
00:13:57,336 --> 00:13:59,213
[music continues]

374
00:13:59,296 --> 00:14:00,172
Sir, Sir, Sir!

375
00:14:00,256 --> 00:14:00,756
Move aside.

376
00:14:00,839 --> 00:14:03,467
- Move! Oh-- sorry, Sir!
- I said move!

377
00:14:04,552 --> 00:14:05,177
[music fades]

378
00:14:05,261 --> 00:14:06,845
- Jay.
- Oka.

379
00:14:06,929 --> 00:14:08,639
- Ms. Shine.
- Oka.

380
00:14:08,722 --> 00:14:10,391
Ms. Audrey!

381
00:14:10,474 --> 00:14:11,308
Ms. Audrey, good mo--

382
00:14:11,392 --> 00:14:13,727
- Jona!
- Oh my!

383
00:14:13,936 --> 00:14:15,813
Why are you with Handsome?
[chuckles]

384
00:14:15,896 --> 00:14:16,730
I’m Oka.

385
00:14:16,814 --> 00:14:18,023
Your new bodyguard?

386
00:14:18,107 --> 00:14:19,024
Oh, no.

387
00:14:19,108 --> 00:14:20,317
I just accompanied him.

388
00:14:20,401 --> 00:14:22,069
Oh gosh, oh gosh!

389
00:14:23,404 --> 00:14:24,071
- Audrey!
- Sir!

390
00:14:24,154 --> 00:14:24,947
Where's the proposal…

391
00:14:25,030 --> 00:14:26,323
… for our activity

392
00:14:26,407 --> 00:14:27,950
with the weavers' community?

393
00:14:28,534 --> 00:14:30,244
I've been looking for it for a while!

394
00:14:30,327 --> 00:14:31,704
It's on your desk.

395
00:14:32,246 --> 00:14:33,747
I finished it last night,

396
00:14:33,831 --> 00:14:35,958
because I’m just working half-day today.

397
00:14:36,041 --> 00:14:38,127
My shift is supposed to start later.

398
00:14:38,711 --> 00:14:39,461
Is that so?

399
00:14:40,129 --> 00:14:41,589
So, what are you doing here?

400
00:14:42,172 --> 00:14:43,716
Ah, I just accompanied him.

401
00:14:43,799 --> 00:14:45,593
Ah-- ah, Sir, this is Oscar.

402
00:14:45,676 --> 00:14:47,261
He's the one applying as driver.

403
00:14:47,761 --> 00:14:49,179
Oscar: Oscar, Sir.

404
00:14:49,263 --> 00:14:49,805
Oscar Asuncion,

405
00:14:49,889 --> 00:14:50,723
but just call me Oka,

406
00:14:50,806 --> 00:14:51,765
at your service.

407
00:14:52,349 --> 00:14:53,475
I'm very careful when I work,

408
00:14:53,559 --> 00:14:54,476
and when I drive.

409
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:56,854
[pensive music playing]

410
00:14:59,648 --> 00:15:01,775
He's my husband's friend.

411
00:15:02,318 --> 00:15:04,445
He can be trusted, Sir.

412
00:15:05,571 --> 00:15:07,156
Then he'll be trusted.

413
00:15:07,239 --> 00:15:09,283
[music continues]

414
00:15:09,366 --> 00:15:10,784
- Take care of that.
- Ouch.

415
00:15:10,868 --> 00:15:13,704
[music continues]

416
00:15:17,041 --> 00:15:20,252
Please bear with Mr. Tinio.

417
00:15:20,336 --> 00:15:21,754
Uhm, don't worry.

418
00:15:21,837 --> 00:15:23,797
He doesn't join the outreach activities.

419
00:15:23,881 --> 00:15:25,382
He just stays here in the office.

420
00:15:25,466 --> 00:15:26,842
It's nothing, it's okay.

421
00:15:28,010 --> 00:15:29,345
He's the boss, after all.
[chuckles]

422
00:15:30,137 --> 00:15:32,097
And I know how to adjust.

423
00:15:32,181 --> 00:15:33,891
Oh! There, that, that, that!

424
00:15:33,974 --> 00:15:37,061
That's the attitude, Ms. Audrey.

425
00:15:37,770 --> 00:15:39,813
Uhm, I'll go ahead.

426
00:15:39,897 --> 00:15:42,775
I don't want to miss the kids' audition.

427
00:15:43,275 --> 00:15:44,360
Jona, you take care of--

428
00:15:44,443 --> 00:15:45,069
Of course.

429
00:15:45,152 --> 00:15:45,986
You'll be late, Ms. Audrey.

430
00:15:46,070 --> 00:15:46,904
Hurry up!

431
00:15:46,987 --> 00:15:48,781
- Bye, Ms. Audrey!
- Okay, bye.

432
00:15:51,617 --> 00:15:52,701
Hey, are you okay?

433
00:15:52,785 --> 00:15:53,786
That was quite strong.

434
00:15:53,869 --> 00:15:56,163
Ouch. It does hurt.

435
00:15:56,246 --> 00:15:58,707
Ah, just kidding. Oh, give me that.

436
00:15:58,791 --> 00:16:01,794
Okay. I'll show you
our service vehicle here.

437
00:16:03,003 --> 00:16:03,879
Oh, Emerson?

438
00:16:04,380 --> 00:16:05,172
Emerson on the phone: 'Toy.

439
00:16:05,255 --> 00:16:07,341
I have a lead on Uno's location.

440
00:16:08,217 --> 00:16:09,134
Really?

441
00:16:09,218 --> 00:16:12,513
He rode in the laundry shop's service.

442
00:16:12,596 --> 00:16:13,847
'Toy, Uno is wounded,

443
00:16:13,931 --> 00:16:15,641
Emerson: it seems he needs our help.

444
00:16:15,724 --> 00:16:16,475
Oh no, what do we do?

445
00:16:16,558 --> 00:16:19,269
I'm on my way to Janine and
Ibyang’s school now,

446
00:16:19,353 --> 00:16:20,771
they have an audition.

447
00:16:20,854 --> 00:16:22,231
Oh, wait. What about Uno?

448
00:16:22,314 --> 00:16:23,440
Am I the only one going?

449
00:16:24,108 --> 00:16:24,692
It would be okay,

450
00:16:24,775 --> 00:16:26,568
but I don’t know anything about first aid.

451
00:16:26,652 --> 00:16:29,196
[suspicious music playing]

452
00:16:29,279 --> 00:16:29,947
Okay, okay, okay, okay.

453
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:30,531
I'll go there.

454
00:16:30,614 --> 00:16:31,615
Send me the address.

455
00:16:31,699 --> 00:16:33,075
Okay, okay, okay.

456
00:16:33,158 --> 00:16:34,034
Okay.

457
00:16:34,118 --> 00:16:35,244
[car engine starts]

458
00:16:35,327 --> 00:16:36,745
[music continues]

459
00:16:37,538 --> 00:16:39,039
[muffled chattering]

460
00:16:46,088 --> 00:16:47,381
Is that Tatoy?

461
00:16:48,173 --> 00:16:49,466
Is he coming?

462
00:16:50,217 --> 00:16:51,260
Ah…

463
00:16:51,802 --> 00:16:53,262
Ibyang, Janine,

464
00:16:54,054 --> 00:16:56,306
your Daddy Tatoy might be late.

465
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:58,058
He said he'll catch up.

466
00:16:59,101 --> 00:17:00,394
But why?

467
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:02,563
He didn't say.

468
00:17:03,689 --> 00:17:07,067
Maybe he has a last-minute client.

469
00:17:07,151 --> 00:17:07,776
You know,

470
00:17:07,860 --> 00:17:10,154
your Tatoy is working double now because…

471
00:17:10,237 --> 00:17:12,406
he's sending the two of you to school.

472
00:17:12,489 --> 00:17:13,115
Yes.

473
00:17:13,198 --> 00:17:15,659
Oh, too bad because…

474
00:17:15,743 --> 00:17:17,828
we really wanted him to watch

475
00:17:17,911 --> 00:17:19,455
what we practiced at home.

476
00:17:20,873 --> 00:17:21,498
Hailey: It's okay.

477
00:17:21,582 --> 00:17:22,791
Don't be sad.

478
00:17:22,875 --> 00:17:23,834
My parents too,

479
00:17:23,917 --> 00:17:25,169
they don't watch my shows.

480
00:17:25,252 --> 00:17:27,546
So, Nana is the one who takes videos.

481
00:17:28,088 --> 00:17:29,631
[soft drama music playing]

482
00:17:29,715 --> 00:17:31,550
Oh, wow. She made me a nanny.

483
00:17:31,633 --> 00:17:32,760
[playful music playing]

484
00:17:32,843 --> 00:17:35,512
Hey! Smile, you two, come on!

485
00:17:35,596 --> 00:17:37,347
Your performance can't be affected,

486
00:17:37,431 --> 00:17:40,309
and your mommy will come anyway,
it's okay!

487
00:17:40,392 --> 00:17:42,102
Yes, she'll come.

488
00:17:43,103 --> 00:17:43,937
And we're here, look.

489
00:17:44,021 --> 00:17:45,189
- Hmm?
- Karla: Yes.

490
00:17:45,272 --> 00:17:46,273
[music continues]

491
00:17:46,356 --> 00:17:49,026
Leighton: Next for audition,
Team Ja-Ha-Byang!

492
00:17:49,109 --> 00:17:50,486
- Hey, it’s your turn!
- Hurry, go.

493
00:17:50,569 --> 00:17:51,445
Do your best.

494
00:17:51,528 --> 00:17:53,614
- Oh, okay, okay.
- Karla: I'll take a video.

495
00:17:53,697 --> 00:17:56,283
Don't worry.
I'll show it to Big Brother Atoy.

496
00:17:56,366 --> 00:17:57,201
Come on.
[exclaims]

497
00:17:57,284 --> 00:17:58,702
Oh, good luck, baby!

498
00:17:58,786 --> 00:18:01,121
Don't do too well, Janine, okay.

499
00:18:01,205 --> 00:18:02,122
Yes po, Big Sister Karla.

500
00:18:02,206 --> 00:18:03,332
Go, good luck!

501
00:18:03,415 --> 00:18:05,000
[music continues]

502
00:18:05,626 --> 00:18:06,794
Take a video, sis.

503
00:18:06,877 --> 00:18:08,045
I'll take a video.

504
00:18:08,128 --> 00:18:10,756
Let's still do our best
in the audition, okay.

505
00:18:10,839 --> 00:18:12,508
I really want…

506
00:18:12,591 --> 00:18:14,927
us to get into the dance club.

507
00:18:15,511 --> 00:18:18,430
Yes. And when Tatoy watches it,

508
00:18:19,139 --> 00:18:20,474
he'll be happy.

509
00:18:23,060 --> 00:18:25,437
[pensive music playing]

510
00:18:25,521 --> 00:18:26,980
Sorry, girls.

511
00:18:27,564 --> 00:18:28,857
Better luck next time.

512
00:18:29,858 --> 00:18:31,860
[music continues]

513
00:18:33,529 --> 00:18:34,822
Why is it like that?

514
00:18:34,905 --> 00:18:37,032
She was the only one who made a mistake,

515
00:18:37,116 --> 00:18:38,742
but all of us are affected?

516
00:18:39,827 --> 00:18:41,245
I’m sorry.

517
00:18:41,870 --> 00:18:46,208
I told you, the two of us should
have auditioned without her.

518
00:18:46,291 --> 00:18:47,459
Dance club member: You're done, right?

519
00:18:48,710 --> 00:18:49,878
Leave already!

520
00:18:49,962 --> 00:18:52,005
[heavy music playing]

521
00:18:56,176 --> 00:18:57,010
Look at that.

522
00:18:57,719 --> 00:18:58,971
What now?

523
00:18:59,054 --> 00:19:01,723
Just one mistake, it turns out,
and we're all eliminated.

524
00:19:02,391 --> 00:19:03,517
What about Ibyang?

525
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:05,602
[music continues]

526
00:19:05,686 --> 00:19:06,895
I practiced.

527
00:19:06,979 --> 00:19:09,815
I won't make a mistake, promise.

528
00:19:10,566 --> 00:19:11,817
Yes, Hailey!

529
00:19:12,401 --> 00:19:13,819
Ibyang memorized the steps.

530
00:19:14,570 --> 00:19:15,529
Go on, then.

531
00:19:16,572 --> 00:19:18,574
5, 6, 7, 8.

532
00:19:18,657 --> 00:19:21,285
1 and 2. 1 and 2.

533
00:19:22,286 --> 00:19:24,163
2. 1, 2, 3.

534
00:19:24,246 --> 00:19:27,332
Single, single. Double, double.

535
00:19:27,416 --> 00:19:29,918
Single, single. Double, do--

536
00:19:30,002 --> 00:19:31,837
[pensive music playing]

537
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:33,589
Hailey: We have to be sure!

538
00:19:33,672 --> 00:19:35,841
I don't want to be eliminated
because of Ibyang!

539
00:19:35,924 --> 00:19:40,971
Janine, isn't it your dream too to
become a member of the dance club?

540
00:19:42,306 --> 00:19:43,849
Well, sorry.

541
00:19:45,559 --> 00:19:46,977
I'll do better.

542
00:19:47,060 --> 00:19:49,605
When we're on stage, I'll be perfect!

543
00:19:49,688 --> 00:19:51,190
[music continues]

544
00:19:55,527 --> 00:19:56,653
Oh, what? Has it started?

545
00:19:56,737 --> 00:19:58,405
Ja-Ha-Byang is next!

546
00:19:58,488 --> 00:19:59,448
- Come on.
- Hurry!

547
00:19:59,531 --> 00:20:01,408
Where's Atoy?

548
00:20:01,491 --> 00:20:03,619
Ah, I think he has a client.

549
00:20:03,702 --> 00:20:04,453
Huh?

550
00:20:04,536 --> 00:20:06,914
[light music playing]

551
00:20:06,997 --> 00:20:08,332
Leighton: Next auditionees,

552
00:20:08,415 --> 00:20:09,625
Team Ja-Ley!

553
00:20:09,708 --> 00:20:12,753
[audience cheering]

554
00:20:15,422 --> 00:20:17,132
Where's Ibyang?

555
00:20:17,216 --> 00:20:19,551
[hip-hop upbeat music playing]

556
00:20:21,553 --> 00:20:22,262
Where's Ibyang?

557
00:20:22,346 --> 00:20:26,391
[audience cheering]

558
00:20:26,475 --> 00:20:31,688
[music continues]

559
00:20:31,772 --> 00:20:35,859
[soft drama music playing]

560
00:20:44,660 --> 00:20:45,619
JANINE: Ibyang…

561
00:20:46,954 --> 00:20:50,249
you don't really like
the dance club that much, right?

562
00:20:50,832 --> 00:20:54,503
Huh? I-- I like being with you.

563
00:20:54,586 --> 00:20:58,298
If I’m the only one who’ll be affected
when you make a mistake,

564
00:20:58,382 --> 00:20:59,883
it would be okay.

565
00:20:59,967 --> 00:21:00,801
But…

566
00:21:02,761 --> 00:21:04,054
what about Hailey?

567
00:21:05,055 --> 00:21:07,224
[music continues]

568
00:21:08,392 --> 00:21:09,601
Let's do this.

569
00:21:10,686 --> 00:21:12,980
Let's improve your…

570
00:21:13,605 --> 00:21:17,609
steps first, your dance skills.

571
00:21:17,693 --> 00:21:20,696
Then, we'll help you audition next time.

572
00:21:20,779 --> 00:21:21,697
Okay?

573
00:21:21,780 --> 00:21:22,281
Ah--

574
00:21:22,364 --> 00:21:23,365
Janine: Yes?

575
00:21:23,448 --> 00:21:24,741
Uhm…

576
00:21:24,825 --> 00:21:26,368
[music continues]

577
00:21:26,451 --> 00:21:27,119
Oh, okay.

578
00:21:29,037 --> 00:21:30,038
Thank you!

579
00:21:30,122 --> 00:21:33,709
[music continues]

580
00:21:35,544 --> 00:21:37,170
Leighton: Next for audition,

581
00:21:37,254 --> 00:21:38,755
Team Ja-Ha-Byang!

582
00:21:39,339 --> 00:21:40,549
We're now Team Ja-Ley.

583
00:21:40,632 --> 00:21:41,967
Janine, let's go!

584
00:21:42,509 --> 00:21:43,593
Let's go.

585
00:21:44,219 --> 00:21:45,178
[music fades]

586
00:21:46,805 --> 00:21:49,224
[melodramatic music playing]

587
00:21:55,314 --> 00:21:59,234
[audience cheering]

588
00:21:59,318 --> 00:22:01,737
[music continues]

589
00:22:02,738 --> 00:22:03,655
Dance club member: Kid…

590
00:22:04,823 --> 00:22:06,199
[music fades]

591
00:22:06,283 --> 00:22:08,660
Those who aren't auditioning
aren't allowed here.

592
00:22:09,619 --> 00:22:11,955
Go watch with the audience.

593
00:22:12,539 --> 00:22:13,582
I’m sorry.

594
00:22:13,665 --> 00:22:16,793
[melodramatic music playing]

595
00:22:19,838 --> 00:22:22,174
Miss, uhm…

596
00:22:22,257 --> 00:22:23,633
do you recognize this person?

597
00:22:23,717 --> 00:22:24,468
Atoy: Have you seen him?

598
00:22:24,551 --> 00:22:25,427
Maybe…

599
00:22:25,510 --> 00:22:28,055
he was your customer or
maybe your employee here.

600
00:22:28,138 --> 00:22:28,638
There, look.

601
00:22:28,722 --> 00:22:30,724
Oh, we don't have an employee
who looks like that,

602
00:22:30,807 --> 00:22:35,562
and we also don't remember
the faces of all our customers.

603
00:22:35,645 --> 00:22:36,772
Mmm-hmm. Really?

604
00:22:36,855 --> 00:22:38,523
Even someone this handsome?

605
00:22:38,607 --> 00:22:39,399
Atoy: There, look.

606
00:22:39,483 --> 00:22:42,110
Look at the face,
he looks like someone from Encantadia.

607
00:22:42,194 --> 00:22:43,403
- Right?
- Yes.

608
00:22:44,446 --> 00:22:46,073
- No one?
- No one.

609
00:22:46,156 --> 00:22:47,157
Mmm.

610
00:22:47,240 --> 00:22:48,533
[sneaky music playing]

611
00:22:48,617 --> 00:22:50,202
Ah, is this your operation center, miss?

612
00:22:50,285 --> 00:22:51,745
Wow, it's so nice!

613
00:22:51,828 --> 00:22:53,330
Can I…

614
00:22:53,413 --> 00:22:55,165
just look around inside for a moment?

615
00:22:55,248 --> 00:22:56,374
[music swells]

616
00:22:56,458 --> 00:22:57,751
Are you a cop?

617
00:22:58,543 --> 00:22:59,503
[music fades]

618
00:22:59,586 --> 00:23:00,837
Ah, you know…

619
00:23:00,921 --> 00:23:02,798
Ah, miss, what's your name again?

620
00:23:02,881 --> 00:23:03,465
It’s Alma.

621
00:23:03,548 --> 00:23:04,382
Alma.

622
00:23:04,466 --> 00:23:05,926
Emerson: You know, Ms. Alma,

623
00:23:06,009 --> 00:23:07,135
it's good that you asked.

624
00:23:07,219 --> 00:23:09,387
Because that's really what I wanted
when I was a kid.

625
00:23:09,471 --> 00:23:11,515
I used to say, “When I grow up,
I want to become a police officer.”

626
00:23:11,598 --> 00:23:15,268
[soft rock music playing]

627
00:23:21,149 --> 00:23:22,484
[music fades]

628
00:23:37,707 --> 00:23:42,337
[tense music playing]

629
00:23:44,673 --> 00:23:47,551
[hissing]

630
00:23:47,634 --> 00:23:51,179
[music continues]

631
00:24:06,862 --> 00:24:10,699
[electronic blipping]
[music swells]

632
00:24:10,782 --> 00:24:14,995
[intense music playing]

633
00:24:15,078 --> 00:24:16,872
[gunshot]

634
00:24:16,955 --> 00:24:18,248
Find him.

635
00:24:18,331 --> 00:24:20,125
- [music swells]
- [clangs]

636
00:24:20,208 --> 00:24:20,834
[theme music playing]

637
00:24:20,917 --> 00:24:21,751
What happened?

638
00:24:21,835 --> 00:24:23,211
Why did it become just Ja-Ley?

639
00:24:23,295 --> 00:24:25,255
What happened to Ja-Ha-Byang?

640
00:24:25,338 --> 00:24:27,007
We decided that…

641
00:24:27,090 --> 00:24:28,425
she'll just audition next time.

642
00:24:28,508 --> 00:24:30,260
But where is she?

643
00:24:30,343 --> 00:24:31,761
Emerson: Maybe this is Uno's.

644
00:24:31,845 --> 00:24:32,804
But where are Samir and the others?

645
00:24:34,181 --> 00:24:35,015
You want me to shoot them, Boss?

646
00:24:36,016 --> 00:24:38,518
I want Atoy to suffer longer.

647
00:24:38,602 --> 00:24:40,312
[“Mamang Sastre” playing]

648
00:24:40,395 --> 00:24:41,396
Son of a thread! Grenade!

649
00:24:41,479 --> 00:24:42,314
[grunts]

650
00:24:42,397 --> 00:24:43,648
[explosion]

651
00:24:43,732 --> 00:24:45,150
[music swells]

652
00:24:45,233 --> 00:24:47,235
Rachel C. Arias
